# SQL Injection Audit — `UserRepository`

## Verdict: 100% of parameters are unsafely interpolated

Every method in this class builds its SQL statement by splicing raw user-supplied values directly into the query string. There is no parameterized binding anywhere.

---

## Unsafe patterns, method by method

### `findByFilter`

| Parameter | Interpolation site |
|-----------|-------------------|
| `organizationId` | `WHERE org_id = '${organizationId}'` |
| `role` | `AND role = '${role}'` |
| `searchTerm` | `name ILIKE '%${searchTerm}%'` and `email ILIKE '%${searchTerm}%'` |

### `updateUserStatus`

| Parameter | Interpolation site |
|-----------|-------------------|
| `status` | `SET status = '${status}'` |
| `updatedBy` | `updated_by = '${updatedBy}'` |
| `userId` | `WHERE id = ${userId}` |

### `bulkUpdateSettings`

| Parameter | Interpolation site |
|-----------|-------------------|
| `orgId` | `WHERE org_id = '${orgId}'` |
| every value in `columnUpdates` | `${col} = '${val}'` (5 values) |

---

## Fixed code

```javascript
class UserRepository {
  constructor(pool) {
    this.pool = pool;
  }

  async findByFilter(organizationId, role, searchTerm) {
    let sql = `SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE org_id = $1`;
    if (role) {
      sql += ` AND role = $2`;
    }
    if (searchTerm) {
      sql += ` AND (name ILIKE $3 OR email ILIKE $3)`;
    }
    const params = [organizationId];
    if (role) params.push(role);
    if (searchTerm) params.push(searchTerm);
    const result = await this.pool.query(sql, params);
    return result.rows;
  }

  async updateUserStatus(userId, status, updatedBy) {
    const query = `UPDATE users SET status = $1, updated_by = $2, updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = $3`;
    return this.pool.query(query, [status, updatedBy, userId]);
  }

  async bulkUpdateSettings(orgId, columnUpdates) {
    const sets = Object.keys(columnUpdates).map((col, i) => `${col} = $${i + 2}`).join(', ');
    const query = `UPDATE organization_settings SET ${sets} WHERE org_id = $1`;
    const params = [orgId, ...Object.values(columnUpdates)];
    return this.pool.query(query, params);
  }
}
```

---

## Why the fix is correct

- **Positional placeholders** (`$1`–`$6`) are bound by the driver; no string concatenation of values.
- **Conditional branches** in `findByFilter` push parameters only when the corresponding clause is present, so the placeholder numbering stays contiguous.
- **`bulkUpdateSettings`** uses `Object.keys`/`Object.values` to build the SET list and the parameter array, guaranteeing the 5 values map to `$2`–`$6`.

No other changes to query structure or semantics are needed.

